# Tracked-vs-regenerable is a DECIDED policy, not per-project taste; every
# ignore below carries its reason. The rule: derived GEOMETRY and verified
# READINGS are cheap to commit and expensive to recompute, so they are
# tracked; the book's own raw text and page images rebuild from source.pdf
# and are not project work, so they are not.

# Page renders and raw OCR text: rebuild from source.pdf with render.py /
# ocr_crop.py; also, data/txt and data/zh are the copyrighted text of the
# book itself, not project work.
data/png/
data/crop/
data/txt/
data/zh/
data/raw/
data/ocr/
data/verify/
data/zh_work/
data/figs/manifest.json
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
SETUP_REPORT.txt

# TRACKED on purpose (listed for the record, do not add ignore rules for
# them): data/noise.txt, data/indent/, data/pagemap/, data/headings.json,
# data/structure.json, data/ocr_fixes.json — derived geometry and the
# crop-verification ledger. A fresh checkout without ocr_fixes.json silently
# reinstates every OCR mangle already paid to fix.
# Also TRACKED: STYLE.local.md (the voice-gate ledger, this book's accumulated
# style evolution; losing it loses that work) and STYLE.md (the composed
# contract, deterministic from the styles/ layers, kept for auditable diffs).
# The styles/ layers themselves are shelf-wide source, always tracked.

# Deliverable artifacts that rebuild from the sources. EXCEPTION: on
# completion, the FINAL deliverable EPUB is committed with
#   git add -f out/<deliverable>
# because branches outlive containers and chat attachments do not.
out/*.epub
out/*_bilingual.md

# Keep source.pdf and committed figure crops (data/figs/*.png) TRACKED.
# If your scan is very large and you would rather not commit it, add:
#   source.pdf

# Voice-gate critique prompt (regenerable QC artifact, like bilinguals; never ships)
out/*_critique_prompt.md
# Session scratch dir
scratch/
